<Base title="Privacy policy | CognitioLab" description="How the CognitioLab website handles visitor data, including Google Analytics cookies and your choices.">
  <article class="article">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <div class="post-meta">Last updated 2 November 2026</div>

    <p>This policy covers the CognitioLab website, thecognitiolab.com. Each of our Shopify apps has its own privacy policy, linked from its Shopify App Store listing.</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>If you accept cookies, we use Google Analytics to see how visitors use this site, such as which pages are viewed, roughly where visitors are, and what device they use. This sets cookies in your browser and sends this usage data to Google. If you decline, Google Analytics does not load.</p>
    <p>We store your choice in your browser. You can change it at any time using <a href="#" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</a>, also found in the footer.</p>

    <h2>Emails</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you include in your message. We use them to reply to you.</p>

    <h2>Services this site loads from</h2>
    <p>Like most websites, this site loads some content from other companies, which receive your IP address and basic browser details when that happens:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google Fonts, for the fonts on every page.</li>
      <li>Shopify, for app icons and screenshots.</li>
      <li>YouTube, for videos on product pages. We use its privacy-enhanced mode.</li>
      <li>Cloudflare, which hosts this site.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask for a copy of your data, or to have it corrected or deleted. To make a request or ask a question, email us at <a href="mailto:cognitiolab1@gmail.com">cognitiolab1@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we will update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
